From bc306b4b898ee1475e08178eca25954c4eee1615 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1vivy <1vivy@tutanota.com>
Date: Sun, 28 Jun 2026 02:36:02 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 11/19] camera: ship libHeifWinBufExchg-jni.so to restore
 Live/Motion Photo
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Live/Motion Photo captured a plain JPEG with no embedded motion clip. The
OplusCamera live-photo path drives OplusCameraManager.nativtSendToProcessHeif,
which dlopens libHeifWinBufExchg-jni — the HEIF HW-buffer-exchange carrier that
muxes the FRC-interpolated clip into the still. That blob was missing from the
camera proprietary list, so OplusCameraManager.checkLoadLibrary() silently
swallowed the load failure and the pipeline reported success while embedding
nothing.

Add system_ext/lib64/libHeifWinBufExchg-jni.so. Its NEEDED deps
(libHeifEncoderWrapper, libNativeWinBuffExchange, std libs) already ship, so no
DISABLE_CHECKELF is required. Device-verified via a /system_ext overlay: a live
photo now writes a 17.4 MB JPEG carrying the embedded MP4 (ftyp/moov/mdat) plus
the GCamera:MotionPhoto XMP + GContainer items, recognized as a motion photo.

The LivePhotoPresenter ImageReader.nativeGetConsumer NoSuchMethodException is a
benign fallback symptom (it fires on stock OOS too) — not the cause, and needs
no frameworks_base change.
---
 proprietary-files.txt | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/proprietary-files.txt b/proprietary-files.txt
index d379afa..75e3fae 100644
--- a/proprietary-files.txt
+++ b/proprietary-files.txt
@@ -57,6 +57,7 @@ my_product/product_overlay/framework/com.oplus.camera.unit.sdk.adapter.jar:syste
 my_product/product_overlay/framework/com.oplus.camera.unit.sdk.jar:system_ext/framework/com.oplus.camera.unit.sdk.jar
 system_ext/lib64/libpenguin.so:vendor/lib64/libpenguin.so
 system_ext/lib64/libHeifEncoderWrapper.so
+system_ext/lib64/libHeifWinBufExchg-jni.so
 system_ext/lib64/libNativeWinBuffExchange.so
 system_ext/lib64/liboplusheifwriter.so
 system_ext/priv-app/OplusAppPlatform/OplusAppPlatform.apk
